# Within code/checks/, only the parts later weeks actually depend on are tracked
# (the phantom test suite + the vendored official scorer). validate.py and
# its run outputs are Week-1-specific verification, not needed by git.
code/checks/validate.py
code/checks/outputs/

# Per-run logs. Written fresh on every execution and named by date, so they
# accumulate one file per script per day — exactly the pattern CLAUDE.md
# Section 5.4 rules out. They stay on disk as the debugging record for the
# current run (Section 5.6 still requires them), they just aren't history:
# every number they contain is already in the QC CSVs and the subject index,
# which ARE tracked and carry provenance sidecars.
#
# Applied uniformly, including the two Week 1 logs under code/metadata/outputs/ that
# predate this rule — those were untracked with `git rm --cached` in the same
# commit that added this line, and remain on disk.
*.log

# Model checkpoints (~30 MB each, 416 MB total).
# Regenerable from committed code plus the frozen seed in code/metadata/config.py,
# so they are local working files, not reproducibility artefacts. The training
# HISTORY (route_c_history_*.json) and the SCORES (*_scores.csv) are committed —
# those are the evidence; the weights are just the cache.
code/segmentation/outputs/checkpoints/
code/segmentation/outputs/checkpoints_preaug/
*.pt

# Weekly reports — the user keeps these out of version control deliberately.
reports/
